content.text:
Host is in game but lobby still visible! enterGame should hide lobby. Why still? Maybe host onLobby callback fires after enterGame and `ui.showLobby` because the lobby element is "hidden"? Wait main onLobby:

```
if (!mp) return;
const lobby = ui.el.lobby;
if (!mp.isHost && !mp.hostId) return;
if (!lobby || lobby.classList.contains('hidden')) ui.showLobby(mp.room, players);
else ui.updateLobby(players, meta);
```

When host starts, `startMultiplayerGame` -> buildGame -> attachGame -> `ui.enterGame` hides lobby. Then `mp.tick` every 1.6s calls `_emitLobby`; onLobby sees lobby hidden -> calls `ui.showLobby`, which brings back the lobby screen during gameplay! That's a major bug. It happens after 1.6 sec. Indeed host is in game but lobby visible. Also client, once in game, its `mp._lobbyTimer` emit and onLobby will show lobby again. Need fix: UI should not show lobby after game started. In main onLobby, if game exists and not game.dead, skip lobby UI. Or mp.started. Let's modify main's onLobby:

```
if (!mp) return;
if (game && !game.dead) return; // partida em andamento
...
```

But host could be in game, lobby events ignored. Client join only before game. Good. Also if a new client joins during game, it will handle? For now no late join support. Fine.

Alternatively UI.showLobby if !this.game. Let's fix in main onLobby. Also maybe `ui.updateLobby` only if lobby visible.

Also when client starts, same.

Let's edit main.js onLobby.

